prompt:
你是短剧编剧。根据以下材料制作分集大纲。
原作或创意：{{故事文本}}
类型与观众：{{类型、目标观众}}
制作目标：{{集数、单集大致时长、横竖屏；未定项注明未定}}
必须保留：{{人物关系、关键事件、世界规则、结局或原文台词}}
先提炼主角目标、阻力、人物关系与核心悬念，再按因果推进划分集数，不把原文章节直接当作集数。每集列出开场处境、人物选择、冲突升级、信息揭示与集尾未解决的问题。让反转有铺垫，避免靠巧合解决冲突。最后列出可合并的场景、主要人物与叙事道具，以及改编新增内容和待确认项。本轮只交付文字，不生成媒体。

en.prompt:
Act as a short-drama screenwriter. Develop an episode outline from these materials.
Story or premise: {{source text}}
Genre and audience: {{genre and audience}}
Production goal: {{episode count, approximate episode duration, aspect ratio; mark undecided items}}
Preserve: {{relationships, key events, world rules, ending or verbatim dialogue}}
Identify the protagonist's goal, resistance, relationships and central unanswered question. Divide episodes by cause and effect rather than source chapter numbers. For each episode, state the opening situation, consequential choice, escalating conflict, reveal and unresolved closing question. Seed reversals and avoid coincidence solving the conflict. Finish with opportunities to reuse locations, a cast and narrative-prop list, adaptation additions and open decisions. Deliver text only in this round.

prompt:
根据大纲写一集可拍摄的短剧剧本。
本集大纲：{{大纲}}
人物与前情：{{人物关系、上一集结束状态}}
本集目标：{{时长建议、核心情绪、结尾悬念}}
固定设定：{{时代、场景、人物动机及必须保留的台词}}
按场次组织，以「场次号 / 内外景 / 地点 / 日夜」开头。动作写观众能看到或听到的事实；对白标明说话人，区分现场对白、画外音与内心独白。让动作与对白交替推动关系变化，删去重复解释。保留关键台词原文，不把剧本塞成运镜术语表。列出每场开场状态与结束变化，检查前因后果、道具去向和台词是否能在建议时长内自然说完；估时注明为建议。只输出剧本与少量待确认项。

en.prompt:
Write one shootable short-drama episode.
Outline: {{episode outline}}
Cast and prior events: {{relationships and previous ending state}}
Episode goal: {{suggested duration, central emotion, ending question}}
Established facts: {{period, locations, motivations and exact lines to preserve}}
Organize scenes under scene number / interior or exterior / location / day or night. Write actions as things the audience can see or hear. Name each speaker and distinguish in-scene dialogue, voiceover and internal monologue. Alternate action and dialogue to change relationships and remove redundant exposition. Preserve required lines verbatim. Avoid turning the screenplay into a camera glossary. Record each scene's opening state and resulting change. Check causality, prop ownership and natural delivery time; label duration estimates as suggestions. Output the screenplay and a brief list of unresolved decisions.

prompt:
从以下剧本提炼影视角色设定，不生成图片。
剧本：{{文本}}
视觉方向：{{写实、动画或其他方向}}
给角色分配稳定编号 C01、C02……。每位角色写清：叙事作用与动机、年龄段与体态、脸型与辨识特征、发型发色、基础服装与鞋、关系及声音表演方向。将「固定外貌」「按场次变化的服装或伤痕」「逐镜变化的持物、手势、视线」分开。为固定外貌和每套造型各写一条可原样复用的简短视觉描述，避免相互矛盾。列出正面全身基准图、侧面、背面、表情或细节图的实际需求；道具单独建档，不靠始终拿在手里定义身份。原文未给出的设计标为创作建议，不伪造已存在的参考图。

en.prompt:
Extract a film character bible without generating images.
Screenplay: {{text}}
Art direction: {{live action, animation or other direction}}
Assign stable IDs C01, C02 and so on. For each character describe story function, motivation, age range, build, face and distinguishing features, hair, base clothing and shoes, relationships, and vocal performance. Separate fixed appearance, scene-specific costume or injury changes, and per-shot hands, props and eyelines. Write a short reusable visual phrase for identity and each costume state. List needed front full-body, profile, back, expression and detail references. Catalogue props separately; do not define identity by permanently holding a prop. Label additions not supported by the source as design suggestions, and do not invent existing reference images.

prompt:
担任影视美术统筹，拆解以下剧本的制作资产。
剧本：{{文本}}
已有人物与素材：{{已有设定或资产清单，没有则写无}}
沿用已有编号，新人物用 C、场景用 S、道具用 P 编号。分别列出名称、可见特征、出现的场次、叙事用途、状态变化与需要的参考图。场景记录门窗、主要陈设、出入口、人物可活动区域、主光方向及需要的正反机位；道具记录尺寸参照、材质、持有人及完整、打开、破损等状态。区分已有资产和待制作资产，同一物件不同称呼合并，实质不同的造型保留变体。给出先角色基准、再场景与道具、再镜头图的依赖顺序，不生成素材、不假设图片已存在。

en.prompt:
Act as a film art coordinator and break down this screenplay.
Screenplay: {{text}}
Existing designs and assets: {{inventory or none}}
Reuse established IDs; use C for characters, S for locations and P for props. Record each item's name, visible features, scenes, narrative function, state changes and required images. For locations include doors, windows, major fixtures, entrances, blocking areas, key-light direction and reverse coverage. For props include scale, material, owner and intact, open or damaged states. Distinguish existing assets from work to create. Merge aliases for the same item while retaining genuinely different states. Give a dependency order from character anchors through locations and props to shot images. Do not generate media or pretend references exist.

prompt:
将剧本拆成可执行的分镜表。
剧本：{{文本}}
角色与场景设定：{{设定}}
画幅与目标时长：{{要求}}
按剧情顺序为镜头编号 EP01-SH001……。每镜写明：叙事信息、场景和角色编号、景别与机位、开场构图和人物站位、动作过程、结束状态、对白或音效、建议时长、与相邻镜头的衔接。动作具体到谁用哪只手拿什么、看向何处、从哪里移动到哪里。对白保留说话人和原文，考虑自然语速及反应停顿，不强行压缩到固定秒数。将每镜的「首帧图片提示词」和「动作视频提示词」单独列出；首帧只描述一个瞬间，视频描述状态变化。保持轴线、视线、道具与光源连续，明确有意跳时或换场。本轮只拆分镜，不生成媒体。

en.prompt:
Break this screenplay into an executable shot list.
Screenplay: {{text}}
Character and location bible: {{designs}}
Aspect ratio and target duration: {{requirements}}
Number shots EP01-SH001 onward in story order. Include narrative information, location and character IDs, framing and camera position, opening composition and blocking, action, ending state, dialogue or sound, suggested duration and transition. Specify which hand holds what, eyelines and movement paths. Preserve speakers and exact lines with natural delivery and reaction pauses. Provide separate first-frame image and motion-video prompts for each shot. An image describes one instant; a video describes change. Preserve axis, eyelines, props and light direction. Mark intentional time jumps or scene changes. Deliver planning text only.

prompt:
为下面的对话场次设计开场调度与正反打。
场次：{{剧本}}
空间与陈设：{{场景说明或参考图信息}}
人物与情绪关系：{{角色设定}}
先用简短文字平面图标记门窗、桌椅、出入口、角色初始位置及朝向，区分从场景平面和从摄影机看到的左右。建立人物关系轴线与主机位，设计全景、双方近景、过肩及必要的反应或道具特写；每个机位说明新增信息和使用时机。记录眼线方向、肩位、进出画方向、持物手与主光来源。有人移动越轴时说明重建空间的镜头。为每个必要镜头给一条首帧描述，不为增加镜头而重复同一信息。没有场景图时把站位标为待视觉核对的方案。

en.prompt:
Plan opening blocking and shot/reverse-shot coverage.
Scene: {{screenplay}}
Space and fixtures: {{description or reference details}}
Characters and emotional relationship: {{designs}}
Start with a simple text floor plan showing doors, windows, furniture, entrances, starting positions and facing directions. Distinguish floor-plan directions from camera-relative left and right. Establish the interaction axis and master camera, then choose useful wide, close, over-shoulder, reaction and prop coverage. Explain what information each angle reveals and when to use it. Track eyelines, foreground shoulders, entrances and exits, holding hands and key-light source. Explain how to re-establish an intentional axis crossing. Supply one opening-frame description per necessary shot. Avoid redundant coverage. Without location images, mark the layout as provisional.

prompt:
润色这段影视对白。
原文：{{对白及上下文}}
人物目标和关系：{{设定}}
需要保留的原句：{{原句或无}}
为每人明确当下想从对方得到什么、在隐藏什么。保留剧情信息与人物动机，减少双方都知道的说明性台词，让打断、停顿、回避视线、拿放道具等可见行为承载潜台词。输出一版可拍场景，再简要说明关键修改。将可见说话、画外音和内心独白分开；不要用长段旁白覆盖人物表演，不加入未经要求的口头禅、喊叫或反转。若台词量与目标镜长冲突，提出拆镜或延长建议，不承诺逐字口型同步。

en.prompt:
Polish this film dialogue.
Original scene: {{dialogue and context}}
Objectives and relationship: {{facts}}
Lines to preserve: {{verbatim lines or none}}
Identify what each speaker wants and conceals. Preserve plot and motivations while removing exposition both people know. Use interruptions, pauses, avoided eyelines and prop interactions to carry subtext. Deliver a shootable revised scene and brief reasons for key changes. Distinguish visible speech, off-screen voice and internal monologue. Avoid covering performance with narration or adding unsolicited catchphrases, shouting or twists. If the words do not fit the shot, suggest splitting or extending it rather than promising exact lip synchronization.

prompt:
审查下列剧本、分镜和提示词之间的连戏与可生成性。
设定：{{角色、场景、道具设定}}
分镜与提示词：{{内容}}
已有结果或反馈：{{真实观察，没有则写无}}
逐镜比较上一镜结束状态与下一镜开始状态：人物身份与服装、伤痕、站位和视线、持物手及道具状态、地标和光位、对白说话人、时间与天气。找出单张图描述多个时刻、单镜堆叠互斥运镜、对白放不下、参考图角色不明确等问题。输出「镜号 / 证据 / 影响 / 最小修改」，保留有意跳切及创作选择。区分文字中能发现的问题、需要看成品才能判断的问题和仅为建议的取舍。没有实际成品时不得声称已审片通过，不自动重生成。

en.prompt:
Review continuity and generation feasibility.
Bible: {{characters, locations and props}}
Shots and prompts: {{content}}
Observed results: {{verified observations or none}}
Compare each ending with the next opening: identity, costume, injuries, blocking, eyelines, hands and prop state, landmarks, lighting, speaker, time and weather. Flag still images describing multiple moments, contradictory camera moves, overcrowded dialogue and unclear reference roles. Report shot ID / evidence / impact / smallest useful correction. Respect intentional jump cuts and artistic choices. Separate text-demonstrable problems from issues requiring footage and optional suggestions. Without real outputs, do not claim a completed footage review. Do not regenerate automatically.

prompt:
为这些已生成或已拍摄的镜头制作剪辑交接单。
剧本与镜头顺序：{{内容}}
实际素材及观察：{{片段名称、可用区间、已核实问题}}
音频与字幕要求：{{已有素材和要求}}
按镜号列出真实素材、建议入出点及理由、承接动作或声桥、对白归属、字幕原文、待补镜头和缺失素材。没有实测信息的时间点明确标注待外部核对，不能假装看过或分析过未提供的音视频。字幕沿用剧本，不从画面猜台词。输出顺序与声音层次建议，不把镜头排列当作已完成拼接，不宣称已经调色、混音、提取末帧或导出成片。

en.prompt:
Prepare an edit handoff.
Screenplay and shot order: {{content}}
Actual media and observations: {{clip names, usable ranges and verified issues}}
Audio and subtitle requirements: {{existing assets and requirements}}
For each shot list the real source, suggested in/out points with reasons, action or sound bridge, speaker, exact subtitle text, pickups and missing media. Mark unmeasured timecodes for external verification. Do not pretend to have viewed unavailable footage. Take subtitles from the screenplay rather than guessing speech. Deliver sequencing and sound-layer recommendations without claiming completed stitching, grading, mixing, final-frame extraction or a rendered film.

